# evidence-for: FR-005, AC-008, NFR-001
# evidence-volatile: \d+\.\d+s
# evidence-volatile: Installed \d+ packages in \d+ms
# evidence-volatile: _sneaky_cycle_reader:\d+
# evidence-timeout: 300
#
# D-066 -- the guard that closed D-059's class was itself an instance of it.
#
# test_every_state_cycle_read_goes_through_a_guarded_reader DERIVED its members
# within a directory (glob every *.py, no hand-kept list) but TYPED the
# directory: `Path(fo.__file__).resolve().parent`, i.e. foundry_mcp/tools only.
# The one module that scope omitted is the one its own rationale argues hardest
# for. server.py owns _DISPATCH and the list_tools/call_tool handlers, so it is
# MORE "the MCP request path, where a raise wedges a live run" than tools/ is;
# it carries zero total cycle readers of its own, so the docstring's third
# reason for staying narrow (widening "would mean allow-listing three more
# reader names here") never applied to it either; and it is a file this casting
# already owns, so the fourth (coupling to files it does not own) does not
# apply. It simply was not in the enumeration.
#
# Below, one mutation drives both halves of the claim on the same tree. A raw
# read of state.json["cycle"] -- reached by json.loads(...read_text()), the
# exact non-_load_json route the detector exists to catch -- is appended to
# server.py, and the two membership rules are run over it side by side:
#
#   the tools/ directory literal returns []            <- the defect, GREEN
#   membership derived over the package NAMES the site <- the fix, RED
#
# The detector was never the problem, which is why the same function appended
# to tools/foundry_spawn.py was caught before this fix; the directory literal
# was. Membership is now derived on BOTH axes -- the files in a directory and
# the directories in the package -- per cycle 4's standing instruction to close
# these by derivation rather than by adding the missing member. The boundary is
# the installed package (root + every subpackage), stated with its reasons in
# the guard's docstring; the two offline readers under plugins/foundry/scripts/
# stay outside it structurally, being in neither this package nor the wheel.
#
# GUARDED_CYCLE_READERS is unchanged: widening the scan added no new reader to
# sanction, only new places to look.
#
# The mutation is applied to a mktemp snapshot and restored in the same command;
# the empty `git status --porcelain` line below is the proof the tree is left
# byte-identical.

